Flow Sequencer is two kinds of work under two licences: the code, and the pose drawings.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. The pose drawings
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The pose drawings are the shapes in src/data/poseArt.ts and everything made from them:
the drawings in the app and on its pages, and the SVG files the poses page downloads.

Copyright © 2026 Graham Hagenah. All rights reserved, except as below.

You may download the drawings and use them for your own personal, non-commercial
purposes: your own practice, notes, or a class handout you give away for free.

You may not, without written permission:
  - sell them, alone or as part of anything else;
  - redistribute them, as they are or changed, in bulk or as a set;
  - use them in other apps, websites, products, courses or brands.

The MIT licence below does not cover the drawings, even though their data sits in the
source code. To ask about other uses, open an issue:
https://github.com/grahamhagenah/flow-sequencer/issues

